12383",0,-2,1,"this could be a `static_assert`, no? should the doc comment at the top of the class template state that it may only be used on single-byte data types?"],["09f81acd_a3096d76",1,-2,0,"do we need this? i only see two callers, and it doesn't look like either could pass in null."],["67a7ddf3_7edfee7f",0,-2,0,"https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#noexcept says \"Specify noexcept when it is useful and correct.\" what makes it useful in this context? i'm familiar with using it for move ctors for…"],["788816e4_34afc273",2,-2,1,"`EXPECT_CHECK_DEATH` if this is expecting to hit a `CHECK` (same comment applies below)"],["79544d98_685f5703",1,-2,1,"is this necessary? i understand that it's technically correct, but is there some reason that plain-old `0` will no longer work? i'd be inclined to revert this and similar changes if they're not…"],["82585421_d2a6fb04",0,-2,1,"i'm a bit surprised that this isn't a const reference since this is a `const` method. not sure if that's intentional, or if it would require fixing callsites, so feel free not to address since the…"],["8f6f326b_be7733dd",0,-2,1,"could this be constref? it's morally equivalent to a normal copy ctor."],["95f281ad_d46e7192",0,-2,0,"something to consider for a different CL: perhaps we should make `BufferViewBase` more like `base::span` in that the range (but not its contents) is immutable. in other words, remove this method in…"],["ac5ef501_e3198748",3,-2,1,"image_ is a ConstBufferView, can we construct this in some way as a subspan of it ?"],["bfa0cac6_d56d9f4f",0,-2,1,"uber-nit: move this to the top of the `private:` section as per https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Declaration_Order"],["dcf1fdaa_89a32d71",0,-2,1,"nit: \"a reference to\" since the value isn't copied, no?"],["e561bd1d_8761070c",0,-2,1,"`const` method?"]],0,1748],[7609602,20511,4,0.248,0.173,[[3,0]],[],0,1749],[7651295,20523,1652,0.01,0.005,[[4,0.589,944,990],[5,0.097,0,160],[6,0.082,1,137],[7,0.076,0,119],[